      "text": "Day 4 · Breakfast and transfer to the station for the Vistadome train to Aguas Calientes, then a 30-minute bus ride up to Machu Picchu. This Inca city, a maze of finely built stone temples, houses and fountains, is spectacularly set on a ridge between two peaks. Long hidden by dense vegetation, it was brought to international attention by Hiram Bingham in 1911. Guided tour, lunch in the afternoon and return to Cusco by train.",
